# Self-contained Electron application installed as add-on software under /opt (FHS 3.13), which is
# the intended home of a package built outside Debian from the user's own vendor copy.
evnia-precision-center: dir-or-file-in-opt *
# Electron's Chromium statically links its own copies of these libraries.
evnia-precision-center: embedded-library *
# Electron ships its bundled libvulkan as released upstream.
evnia-precision-center: unstripped-binary-or-object *
# koffi's loader module starts with a shebang but is only ever require()d.
evnia-precision-center: script-not-executable *
# The udev rules grant the logged-in user access to the monitor's own USB functions (2109:8884,
# 0cf2:a201) for this program. The package is installed from a local file, never from an archive
# whose AppStream catalogue could advertise it for that hardware, so it ships no metainfo.
evnia-precision-center: appstream-metadata-missing-modalias-provide *
# Prebuilt upstream binaries (Electron, usb and koffi prebuilds) are shipped unmodified, as their
# upstreams build them: hardening flags and ELF sections are theirs.
evnia-precision-center: binary-has-unneeded-section *
evnia-precision-center: hardening-no-bindnow *
evnia-precision-center: hardening-no-fortify-functions *
evnia-precision-center: exit-in-shared-library *
evnia-precision-center: spelling-error-in-binary *
# The licence texts and READMEs of the bundled components stay next to them in the self-contained
# /opt tree; debian/copyright points there.
evnia-precision-center: extra-license-file *
evnia-precision-center: package-contains-documentation-outside-usr-share-doc *
# Directory layout of the upstream npm packages (koffi/src/koffi/src, usb/dist/usb).
evnia-precision-center: repeated-path-segment *
